    "q-111838": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111838",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$10{m}^{2}+13m+4=$",
      "worked_solution": "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n10{m}^{2}+13m+4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($10\\times 4=40$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($13$).\n\nSince all coefficients are positive, we only need to consider the positive factor pairs of $40.$\n\nThe positive factor pairs of $40$ are\n\n$$\n(1,40),\\,(2,20),\\,(4,10),\\,(5,8).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(5,8)$ add to $13:$ \n\n$$\n5+8=13\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $5m+8m,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{m}^{2}+13m+4 & = \\\\ 10{m}^{2}+5m+8m+4 & = \\\\ (10{m}^{2}+5m)+(8m+4) & = \\\\ 5m(2m+1)+4(2m+1) & = \\\\ (5m+4)(2m+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111838-a",
